  "notes": [
    "Five existing PT PNGs are retained byte-for-byte with their original source revisions and hashes: CornellBoxStandard, Veach MIS, Matpreview copper, glass and diffuse.",
    "Three generated PNGs supplement the five retained originals: Veach bidir uses source 75b53a619f7de2621b9033685cd1bf373befd609 after the BDPT shading-normal fix; rough glass uses 2a14c1666cfffe429ded2ac201badd8a9c5389e0 after the microfacet fix; smooth plastic uses 52c322216a1fc88fbaf1eb215308af95a9397848, integrated into main by merge 1d807461a30131f17474ef372a83b41572a3bc59.",
    "Depth, reconstruction filter, display mapping and material/normal settings are per-image. Veach bidir uses depth 7 with ACES plus native sRGB; the seven PT images use depth 10 with native legacy gamma 2.2.",
    "Original geometry, cameras, lighting and native aspect ratios were retained. Images were rendered at the recorded dimensions, without resizing, denoising or reference-image substitution.",
    "The original Matpreview archive includes no license file. Its raw/derived geometry, source environment and supplied reference images are not redistributed; only generated PNGs are included.",
    "Matpreview materials are explicit native overrides. Plastic is the native Mitsuba-style smooth layered model with Kd=(0.24,0.771,0.361), Ks=(1,1,1), interior IOR 1.9, exterior IOR 1.000277 and nonlinear=false (linear diffuse compensation). Its PNG is a native Gyunity render, not a Mitsuba/reference image or a claim of pixel-identical reference output.",
    "Linear Float32 HDR renders are retained locally for the three new images only and were verified finite/nonnegative. No linear-HDR validation is claimed for the five retained PNGs.",
    "Residual Monte Carlo noise, fireflies and caustic speckles remain. No exposure adjustment was applied to the two new Matpreview images.",
    "CornellBoxStandard and the Veach scene archives include CC0 source licenses. Earlier gallery files and transport-scenes-1024h.json remain unchanged."
  ],
